Well, my last 3 ascension-worthy characters all met death through various
aspects of my stupidity (2 of them with the Amulet in the Planes), but
finally I got one through. No bones files this time to give an early game
boost, but I had reasonably decent luck with drops, although I was nearly
doomed right from the start. I quaffed the starter potions of extra
healing, and then the first chest I opened on level 1 had a fire trap which
not only knocked me down to 2 hp, but reduced my max down to 7. Making it
to Minetown with only 7 hp for the protection run was...harrowing.
Thankfully the temple was coaligned.

Sokoban had the amulet, and I got a bag a bit later on. No magic lamp to be
found anywhere in the game, however a brass lantern and the PYEC sufficed
(inconvenient, but it worked). An early throne sit dealt with master mind
flayers, and after fighting a couple of liches, a blessed genocide scroll
was used to deal with Ls in a more permenant fashion. I just didn't want to
deal with the hassle this time around.

All my games seem to require some sort of major problem, and this time it
was over-enchanting Grayswandir and vaporizing it, so I had to go through
with Mjollnir as a primary. This became an issue on the
rather...eventful...astral plane.

Right side had Famine, a blessed taming scroll helped a bunch when
something summoned nasties on me, but I still had to burn the E word
against a mind flayer. Middle altar was Death, and man what a giant pain in
the patookus. There was a Ki-Rin in the altar room, and he summoned nasties
as soon as I stepped inside, then the captain summoned as part of that read
a cursed scroll of create monster, and suddenly the ENTIRE ROOM (as well as
substantial leaking into the outside corridor) was filled with stuff. So I
did something I'd never done before in the Astral...I put on a ring of
conflict. With conflict helping to thin the numbers, and the summoned
nasties including a cockatrice who donated his corpse to the cause, I was
able to thin out the crowd and head over to the left to deal with
Pestilence and hit my altar.

Opening the first room, I cast light and threw a blessed stinking cloud
inside, which handily wiped out all the priests and damaged the other stuff
(actually, I did this for all 3 initial areas), but outside was an arc
player monster who bullwhipped my Mjollnir and proceeded to smash my rings
of free action and conflict, as well as a couple of random inventory wands
before my 3rd /odeath zap finally got him. Asshole.

Thankfully, I had gotten some giants spawned around the first two areas, so
Famine and Death were blocked off with boulders to not pester me, and I
grabbed another rubber chicken to statue my way to the left side altar. As
a last little test, I lured Pestilence onto the altar, death beamed him,
and tried to offer his corpse...it didn't even give me the option. There's
an article on the spoiler sites about mollifying deities, and there's a
suggestion about sacrificing the riders by luring them onto your high
altar, but apparently TDTOE, and they didn't leave that as a possibility.

Matuse, neutral female human Tourist


